{"id":"mahabharata-12-189","work":"mahabharata","part":12,"partName":"शान्तिपर्व","partNameEn":"Shanti Parva","unit":189,"title":"एकोननवत्यधिकशततमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 189 · The renouncer's practice","summary":{"en":"Yudhishthira says the four stages and the king's dharma have been explained, and asks how liberation is reached. Bhishma describes how meditation arises from steadiness, and how the pure self, resting in itself, attains the deathless.","kn":"ನಾಲ್ಕು ಆಶ್ರಮ, ರಾಜಧರ್ಮ ಹೇಳಲಾಗಿದೆ, ಮೋಕ್ಷವನ್ನು ಹೇಗೆ ತಲುಪುವುದೆಂದು ಯುಧಿಷ್ಠಿರ ಕೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಸ್ಥಿರತೆಯಿಂದ ಧ್ಯಾನ ಹೇಗೆ ಹುಟ್ಟುತ್ತದೆ, ಶುದ್ಧ ಆತ್ಮ ತನ್ನಲ್ಲೇ ನೆಲೆಸಿ ಅಮೃತತ್ವ ಹೇಗೆ ಪಡೆಯುತ್ತದೆಂದು ಭೀಷ್ಮ ವರ್ಣಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"युधिष्ठिर कहते हैं कि चार आश्रम और राजधर्म बताए जा चुके और पूछते हैं कि मोक्ष कैसे मिले। भीष्म बताते हैं कि स्थिरता से ध्यान कैसे उपजता है और शुद्ध आत्मा स्वयं में स्थित होकर अमृतत्व कैसे पाता है।","te":"నాలుగు ఆశ్రమాలు, రాజధర్మం చెప్పబడ్డాయని, మోక్షం ఎలా పొందాలని యుధిష్ఠిరుడు అడుగుతాడు. స్థిరత్వం నుండి ధ్యానం ఎలా పుడుతుందో, శుద్ధాత్మ తనలో నిలిచి అమృతత్వం ఎలా పొందుతుందో భీష్ముడు వర్ణిస్తాడు.","ta":"நான்கு ஆசிரமங்களும் ராஜதர்மமும் விளக்கப்பட்டன, விடுதலையை எவ்வாறு அடைவது என்று யுதிஷ்டிரர் கேட்க, உறுதியிலிருந்து தியானம் எவ்வாறு பிறக்கிறது, தூய ஆன்மா தன்னில் நிலைத்து அழியாமையை எவ்வாறு அடைகிறது என்று பீஷ்மர் விவரிக்கிறார்.","ml":"നാലു ആശ്രമങ്ങളും രാജധർമ്മവും വിവരിച്ചുവെന്നും, മോക്ഷത്തിൽ എത്തുന്നതെങ്ങനെയെന്നും യുധിഷ്ഠിരൻ പറയുന്നു. സ്ഥിരതയിൽനിന്ന് ധ്യാനം ഉണ്ടാകുന്നതെങ്ങനെയെന്നും, സ്വയം നിലകൊള്ളുന്ന ശുദ്ധാത്മാവ് അമൃതത്വം നേടുന്നതെങ്ങനെയെന്നും ഭീഷ്മർ വിവരിക്കുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 12.189; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Wed Jun 16 2021","sections":[{"title":"मोक्षधर्मपर्व","titleEn":"Mokshadharma Parva (Duties for liberation)","verses":[{"text":"युधिष्ठिर उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Yudhishthira said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"चातुराश्रम्यमुक्तं ते राजधर्मास्तथैव च ।\nनानाश्रयाश्च बहव इतिहासाः पृथग्विधाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"You have told me of the four stages of life and of the duties of kings, and of many kinds of old tales resting on various themes."}},{"n":2,"text":"श्रुतास्त्वत्तः कथाश्चैव धर्मयुक्ता महामते ।\nसंदेहोऽस्ति तु कश्चिन्मे तद्भवान्वक्तुमर्हति ॥","meaning":{"en":"I have heard from you tales joined with righteousness, greatly wise one; but I have a certain doubt, and you should clear it."}},{"n":3,"text":"जापकानां फलावाप्तिं श्रोतुमिच्छामि भारत ।\nकिं फलं जपतामुक्तं क्व वा तिष्ठन्ति जापकाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bharata, I wish to hear what the reciters of prayer attain: what fruit is said to come to those who recite, and where do the reciters stay?"}},{"n":4,"text":"जपस्य च विधिं कृत्स्नं वक्तुमर्हसि मेऽनघ ।\nजापका इति किं चैतत्सांख्ययोगक्रियाविधिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Sinless one, tell me the whole rule of recitation. And what is meant by \"reciters\"? Is it a rule of acts of Sankhya and yoga?"}},{"n":5,"text":"किं यज्ञविधिरेवैष किमेतज्जप्यमुच्यते ।\nएतन्मे सर्वमाचक्ष्व सर्वज्ञो ह्यसि मे मतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Is it only a rule of sacrifice, or is this called something to be recited? Tell me all this, for I think you know everything."}},{"text":"भीष्म उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Bhishma said:"}},{"n":6,"text":"अत्राप्युदाहरन्तीममितिहासं पुरातनम् ।\nयमस्य यत्पुरा वृत्तं कालस्य ब्राह्मणस्य च ॥","meaning":{"en":"On this they cite an ancient tale, what once happened among Yama, Time and a brahmin."}},{"n":7,"text":"संन्यास एव वेदान्ते वर्तते जपनं प्रति ।\nवेदवादाभिनिर्वृत्ता शान्तिर्ब्रह्मण्यवस्थितौ ।\nमार्गौ तावप्युभावेतौ संश्रितौ न च संश्रितौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Renunciation alone is found in the Vedanta with regard to recitation; peace, born of the Vedic teaching, lies in standing in Brahman. Both these paths are resorted to and yet not resorted to."}},{"n":8,"text":"यथा संश्रूयते राजन्कारणं चात्र वक्ष्यते ।\nमनःसमाधिरत्रापि तथेन्द्रियजयः स्मृतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"King, the reason will be told as it is heard. Here too concentration of mind and conquest of the senses are remembered."}},{"n":9,"text":"सत्यमग्निपरीचारो विविक्तानां च सेवनम् ।\nध्यानं तपो दमः क्षान्तिरनसूया मिताशनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Truth, tending the fire, attending the secluded, meditation, austerity, self-control, patience, freedom from envy and moderate eating;"}},{"n":10,"text":"विषयप्रतिसंहारो मितजल्पस्तथा शमः ।\nएष प्रवृत्तको धर्मो निवृत्तकमथो शृणु ॥","meaning":{"en":"withdrawal from the objects of sense, moderate speech and calm: this is the righteousness of action; now hear the righteousness of withdrawal."}},{"n":11,"text":"यथा निवर्तते कर्म जपतो ब्रह्मचारिणः ।\nएतत्सर्वमशेषेण यथोक्तं परिवर्जयेत् ।\nत्रिविधं मार्गमासाद्य व्यक्ताव्यक्तमनाश्रयम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"How action ceases for the celibate who recites: one should leave all this entirely, as described, taking up the threefold path, manifest and unmanifest, without support."}},{"n":12,"text":"कुशोच्चयनिषण्णः सन्कुशहस्तः कुशैः शिखी ।\nचीरैः परिवृतस्तस्मिन्मध्ये छन्नः कुशैस्तथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seated on a heap of kusha grass, with kusha in hand and a topknot tied with kusha, clothed in bark garments, and covered with kusha in the midst of it,"}},{"n":13,"text":"विषयेभ्यो नमस्कुर्याद्विषयान्न च भावयेत् ।\nसाम्यमुत्पाद्य मनसो मनस्येव मनो दधत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"he should bow to the objects of sense without dwelling on them; having produced evenness of mind, he should fix mind within mind."}},{"n":14,"text":"तद्धिया ध्यायति ब्रह्म जपन्वै संहितां हिताम् ।\nसंन्यस्यत्यथ वा तां वै समाधौ पर्यवस्थितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"With that intent, reciting the beneficial collection of verses, he meditates on Brahman, or else renounces even it, firm in concentration."}},{"n":15,"text":"ध्यानमुत्पादयत्यत्र संहिताबलसंश्रयात् ।\nशुद्धात्मा तपसा दान्तो निवृत्तद्वेषकामवान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Meditation arises here through resorting to the power of the recitation; he becomes pure in self, restrained by austerity, free from hatred and desire."}},{"n":16,"text":"अरागमोहो निर्द्वंद्वो न शोचति न सज्जते ।\nन कर्ताकरणीयानां न कार्याणामिति स्थितिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Free from passion and delusion, beyond opposites, he neither grieves nor clings; his state is that he is not the doer of what is to be done or what ought to be done."}},{"n":17,"text":"न चाहंकारयोगेन मनः प्रस्थापयेत्क्वचित् ।\nन चात्मग्रहणे युक्तो नावमानी न चाक्रियः ॥","meaning":{"en":"He should not fix his mind anywhere by egoism, nor be absorbed in seizing on self, nor despise others, nor be inactive."}},{"n":18,"text":"ध्यानक्रियापरो युक्तो ध्यानवान्ध्याननिश्चयः ।\nध्याने समाधिमुत्पाद्य तदपि त्यजति क्रमात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Devoted to the work of meditation, disciplined, a meditator resolved on meditation, having reached concentration in meditation, he gradually gives up even that."}},{"n":19,"text":"स वै तस्यामवस्थायां सर्वत्यागकृतः सुखी ।\nनिरीहस्त्यजति प्राणान्ब्राह्मीं संश्रयते तनुम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"In that state, having renounced everything, he is happy; free of wishes, he gives up his breath and takes a body of Brahman."}},{"n":20,"text":"अथ वा नेच्छते तत्र ब्रह्मकायनिषेवणम् ।\nउत्क्रामति च मार्गस्थो नैव क्वचन जायते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Or he does not wish for the service of that Brahman-body; remaining on the path he departs and is never born anywhere."}},{"n":21,"text":"आत्मबुद्धिं समास्थाय शान्तीभूतो निरामयः ।\nअमृतं विरजःशुद्धमात्मानं प्रतिपद्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Resting in the knowledge of the Self, become calm and free of illness, he reaches the Self, immortal, stainless and pure."}}]}]}